Ptyxis is a modern terminal emulator built for the container era,
designed to seamlessly integrate with GNOME desktop environments.

Key Features:
- Modern GNOME interface built with GTK4 and libadwaita
- Dynamic theming with extensive color palette support
- Smart process tracking (sudo, SSH sessions)
- Advanced tab management with live previews
- Customizable keyboard shortcuts and user profiles
- High-performance rendering with GPU acceleration
- Terminal inspector for debugging
- Encrypted scrollback buffers for enhanced privacy

MIU Darwin-specific notes:
This port targets MIU Darwin, a Darwin/XNU distribution with its own C
library (libmiu, shipped as /usr/lib/libSystem.B.dylib) and its own Wayland
compositor.  It is cross compiled from Fedora against GTK4 4.20.4,
libadwaita 1.8.7 and VTE 0.80.5.

Container integration features (Podman, Toolbox, Distrobox) are not
available, as they require Linux-specific functionality.  Rendering uses the
cairo renderer; there is no GPU acceleration yet.

Unlike the OpenBSD port, wordexp(3) is not disabled: MIU Darwin implements
it in its own C library, so ptyxis_path_expand() takes the normal path.
